---
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import HeartButton from "@plugdash/heartpost/HeartButton.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../../components/InstallCommand.astro";
import PluginReference from "../../components/PluginReference.astro";
import { loadDemoEntry } from "../../data/demo-entry";
import { extendPluginDocToc } from "../../data/doc-toc";
import { getPlugin } from "../../data/plugins";
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const plugin = getPlugin("heartpost")!;
const demo = await loadDemoEntry();
const tocEntries = extendPluginDocToc(
  { id: "options", text: "Options" },
  { id: "known-limits", text: "Known limits" },
);
---

<Doc
  tocEntries={tocEntries}
  currentSlug="heartpost"
  title="heartpost"
  section="@plugdash/heartpost"
  description="A heart counter with one KV row per post."
>
  <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
  <p>
    Keeps one count per post in plugin KV (<code>count:&lt;entry id&gt;</code>),
    so a post with 1,000 hearts is still one row. Whether a reader hearted
    is kept in their own browser (<code>localStorage</code>), so clicking
    again takes the heart back. Ships <code>HeartButton.astro</code>, which
    loads the count only when it comes within 200px of the viewport. A page
    that is never scrolled that far makes no request.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <InstallCommand command={plugin.installCommand} />

  <h2 id="register">Register</h2>
  <p>
    Open <code>astro.config.mjs</code> and add the plugin to the
    <code>plugins</code> array of the <code>emdash()</code> integration.
    Pass the collections whose entries can be hearted. The default is
    <code>["posts"]</code>; the blog template on this site uses
    <code>blog</code>.
  </p>
  <Code language="js" filename="astro.config.mjs" code={`import { defineConfig } from "astro/config"
import emdash from "emdash/astro"
import { heartpostPlugin } from "@plugdash/heartpost"

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    emdash({
      plugins: [
        heartpostPlugin({ collections: ["blog"] }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
})`} />

  <h2 id="add-the-component">Add the component</h2>
  <Code language="astro" code={`---
import HeartButton from "@plugdash/heartpost/HeartButton.astro"
---
<HeartButton post={post} />`} />
  <p>
    Hearts are keyed on <code>post.data.id</code>. Only published entries
    in one of the <code>collections</code> can be hearted; anything else is
    rejected.
  </p>

  <h2 id="live-demo">Live demo</h2>
  {demo ? (
    <div class="demo-inline" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem">
      <HeartButton post={demo} />
      <span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.875rem">The count for a real post on this site. Click again to take the heart back.</span>
    </div>
  ) : (
    <p>The demo post is not published yet.</p>
  )}

  <PluginReference plugin={plugin} />

  <h2 id="options">Options</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>option</th><th>type</th><th>default</th><th>description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>collections</code></td><td><code>string[]</code></td><td><code>["posts"]</code></td><td>Collections whose entries can be hearted</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>rateLimitPerMinute</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>10</code></td><td>Hearts per client IP per minute. <code>0</code> turns the limit off</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>trustProxyHeader</code></td><td><code>string | null</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Header to read the client IP from behind your own proxy</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>label</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>"hearts"</code></td><td>Label for the heart count</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="known-limits">Known limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The count is a soft count, not a vote. Clearing site data or switching browsers lets the same person heart again.</li>
    <li>The built-in rate limit is a speed bump. For a public site, add a platform rate limit (for example a Cloudflare rule) on <code>POST /_emdash/api/plugins/heartpost/heart</code> and <code>heart-remove</code>.</li>
    <li>No admin page for viewing counts. The Heart Post admin page only removes visitor rows left by 0.2.x.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="for-agents">For agents</h2>
  <p>
    After installing @plugdash/heartpost, register
    <code>heartpostPlugin(&#123; collections: [...] &#125;)</code> with the
    site's post collection, import <code>HeartButton.astro</code> in the
    post layout and render
    <code>&lt;HeartButton post=&#123;post&#125; /&gt;</code>. Verify with
    <code>GET /_emdash/api/plugins/heartpost/heart-status?id=&lt;entry id&gt;</code>,
    which returns <code>&#123; success: true, data: &#123; count &#125; &#125;</code>.
    If a click does not raise the count, the heart request was rejected:
    the entry is not published or its collection is not in
    <code>collections</code>. Data stored: one KV row per post,
    <code>count:&lt;entry id&gt;</code>.
  </p>
</Doc>
